<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Western Areas Q1 pre-capex net slumps.</title>
<headline>Western Areas Q1 pre-capex net slumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capex		6.9     vs 48.97</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 68.89   vs 79.36</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			    691,000 vs 737,000</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			 4,391   vs 4,832</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			   6.36    vs 6.56</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			   51,777  vs 48,698</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)			52,890  vs 56,085</p>
<p>Full name: Western Areas Gold Mining Company Ltd, managed by JCI Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that adverse geological conditions were encountered in the SV2/3 87 and 90 level areas, which delayed the completion of reef raises and hampered subsequent production. Output from these areas is being rescheduled to accommodate these conditions.</p>
<p>It added the drive to reduce costs continues and further improvements are expected next quarter.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
